+`lab/e2e-upgrade-release.sh` is the upgrade between real releases (#644) on `lab/docker-compose-upgrade-release.yml` (the FRR edge of `lab/frr` and one Packeteer container) with `lab/packeteer-upgrade-release.yaml` (observe, sqlite, sign-in on). It runs the v1.6.0 image, pinned by digest in the script (`PREV_IMAGE` must contain `@sha256:`), and writes a second user, a pin, a pause, and an acknowledged `provider.down` alert. It stops that container and starts the image built from this tree on the same `packeteer-data` volume (named per compose project, so a local run cannot touch a real one), and checks that `-check` passes, that the pin, pause, acknowledgement, users, event history, and audit log are restored, that the mode is still observe, that no `steering.lost` fired, and that the edge holds no route from Packeteer. Then it does the downgrade: the v1.6.0 image started again on the volume shows the same state (no config key is newer than that release, so none is removed; the README upgrade notes say to remove such keys first). Container exit codes are 0 on SIGTERM. It complements `lab/e2e-upgrade.sh`, which upgrades a build of this tree against a fake release server. CI runs it as the `upgrade-release` job.
 
 GitHub Actions runs the scripts above (except the Routinator lab, which is the `only-invalid` job, and the release upgrade lab, which is the `upgrade-release` job), the walkthrough, and the demo as the `e2e` job. Docker and Go are required (the scripts build `lab/checkroute`, `lab/checkpath`, `lab/checkms`, `lab/checkpop`, `lab/checklease`, and `lab/mkcerts`); they do not run in the unit-test job. `go test ./lab/checkroute ./lab/checkpath ./lab/checkms ./lab/checkpop ./lab/checklease ./lab/doccmds` covers the checks themselves.
 
